<img src="https://api.mehewara.edu.lk/api/v1/media/legacy/supabase-storage/88d5458d-0425-5a68-a5df-bcdc1f2c57cf.unknown" alt="Screenshot 2026-06-17 230638.png" class="mhw-q-img" />', '<p>The figure shows how a horizontal force P is applied on an object placed on a plane. When the value of P is gradually increased from zero, the frictional force (F) acting on the object,</p>
<img src="https://api.mehewara.edu.lk/api/v1/media/legacy/supabase-storage/88d5458d-0425-5a68-a5df-bcdc1f2c57cf.unknown" alt="Screenshot 2026-06-17 230638.png" class="mhw-q-img" />', NULL, 'As force $P$ increases, static friction increases equally to oppose it until it reaches its maximum limit (limiting friction). Once the object overcomes this and starts moving, the friction drops slightly to a constant value known as kinetic (or dynamic) friction.', 'As force $P$ increases, static friction increases equally to oppose it until it reaches its maximum limit (limiting friction). Once the object overcomes this and starts moving, the friction drops slightly to a constant value known as kinetic (or dynamic) friction.', NULL, 'sanitized', 'v1', 4, 'single', 0, 1, 'admin', 'draft', strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ','now')) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET paper_id = excluded.paper_id, number = excluded.number, question_html_en = excluded.question_html_en, question_html_si = excluded.question_html_si, explanation_html_en = excluded.explanation_html_en, explanation_html_si = excluded.explanation_html_si, sanitization_status = excluded.sanitization_status, option_count = excluded.option_count, answer_mode = excluded.answer_mode, is_all_correct = excluded.is_all_correct, state = 'draft', updated_at = excluded.updated_at;
DELETE FROM question_options WHERE question_id = '88292606-863a-5b6a-a761-5801cdcb346c';
UPDATE questions SET state = 'published' WHERE id = '88292606-863a-5b6a-a761-5801cdcb346c';
<img src="https://api.mehewara.edu.lk/api/v1/media/legacy/supabase-storage/83b5f15a-862c-5da5-9df6-596ec1b07b19.unknown" alt="Screenshot 2026-06-17 230934.png" class="mhw-q-img" />', '<p>Arrangements A, B, C and D set up by a student in the laboratory using four clean, iron nails to study about corrosion of iron are as follows.<br>A - Zn plate attached<br>B - distilled water<br>C - vinegar<br>D - Cu plate attached<br><br>When observed after a few days, the nail in which arrangement has corroded least?</p>
<img src="https://api.mehewara.edu.lk/api/v1/media/legacy/supabase-storage/83b5f15a-862c-5da5-9df6-596ec1b07b19.unknown" alt="Screenshot 2026-06-17 230934.png" class="mhw-q-img" />', NULL, 'Zinc ($Zn$) is more reactive than Iron ($Fe$). When attached to iron, zinc acts as a sacrificial anode, undergoing oxidation itself and actively protecting the iron nail from corroding (cathodic protection).', 'Zinc ($Zn$) is more reactive than Iron ($Fe$). When attached to iron, zinc acts as a sacrificial anode, undergoing oxidation itself and actively protecting the iron nail from corroding (cathodic protection).', NULL, 'sanitized', 'v1', 4, 'single', 0, 1, 'admin', 'draft', strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ','now')) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET paper_id = excluded.paper_id, number = excluded.number, question_html_en = excluded.question_html_en, question_html_si = excluded.question_html_si, explanation_html_en = excluded.explanation_html_en, explanation_html_si = excluded.explanation_html_si, sanitization_status = excluded.sanitization_status, option_count = excluded.option_count, answer_mode = excluded.answer_mode, is_all_correct = excluded.is_all_correct, state = 'draft', updated_at = excluded.updated_at;
DELETE FROM question_options WHERE question_id = '8641add0-b104-5f53-b492-e81529e24745';
UPDATE questions SET state = 'published' WHERE id = '8641add0-b104-5f53-b492-e81529e24745';
<img src="https://api.mehewara.edu.lk/api/v1/media/legacy/supabase-storage/1376cd8c-861a-50e1-a803-bd8bd97e428e.unknown" alt="Screenshot 2026-06-17 230955.png" class="mhw-q-img" />', '<p>By connecting a conducting wire between X and Y in the circuit shown in the figure, the bulb in it can be lighted. In three instances, three wires made of the same metal were connected between X and Y as given below and the brightness of the bulb was measured.<br>A - connecting a thin long wire<br>B - connecting a thick short wire<br>C - connecting a thin short wire<br><br>Accordingly, what is the order in which the brightness of the bulb increases?</p>
<img src="https://api.mehewara.edu.lk/api/v1/media/legacy/supabase-storage/1376cd8c-861a-50e1-a803-bd8bd97e428e.unknown" alt="Screenshot 2026-06-17 230955.png" class="mhw-q-img" />', NULL, 'Electrical resistance is directly proportional to wire length and inversely proportional to cross-sectional thickness. Higher resistance results in lower current and lower bulb brightness. Wire A (thin, long) has the highest resistance (lowest brightness). Wire B (thick, short) has the lowest resistance (highest brightness). Thus, brightness increases as A $\rightarrow$ C $\rightarrow$ B.', 'Electrical resistance is directly proportional to wire length and inversely proportional to cross-sectional thickness. Higher resistance results in lower current and lower bulb brightness. Wire A (thin, long) has the highest resistance (lowest brightness). Wire B (thick, short) has the lowest resistance (highest brightness). Thus, brightness increases as A $\rightarrow$ C $\rightarrow$ B.', NULL, 'sanitized', 'v1', 4, 'single', 0, 1, 'admin', 'draft', strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ','now')) ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET paper_id = excluded.paper_id, number = excluded.number, question_html_en = excluded.question_html_en, question_html_si = excluded.question_html_si, explanation_html_en = excluded.explanation_html_en, explanation_html_si = excluded.explanation_html_si, sanitization_status = excluded.sanitization_status, option_count = excluded.option_count, answer_mode = excluded.answer_mode, is_all_correct = excluded.is_all_correct, state = 'draft', updated_at = excluded.updated_at;
